<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Entre Ríos Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Entre Ríos is a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> between the Paraná and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> rivers. In the independence era its caudillos joined Artigas's Federal League, and in 1820 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-ramirez">Francisco Ramírez</a> proclaimed the short-lived Republic of Entre Ríos. It signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-pact">Federal Pact</a> of 1831, and its governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justo-jose-de-urquiza">Justo José de Urquiza</a> overthrew Rosas in 1852.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/entre-rios-province.jpg" alt="Entre Ríos Province" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ANDY ABIR ALAN · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Parana,_Entre_Rios,_Argentina_-_panoramio_(1001).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
